From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Swanson <rswanson05@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:36:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat: jump between agent turns in the scrollback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The server marks a pane's scrollback each time its agent goes idle, at
the top of the agent's prompt area (Claude Code's rule above its ❯
prompt, else the cursor row): where its answer ended and where the
user's next message will be printed. When the agent next starts working
and keys were typed in between, the mark also counts as a message.
Marks are libghostty tracked rows, so they follow new output, reflow
and scrollback pruning, and vanish with their rows.

pane.scroll_to_mark scrolls a pane to the previous or next turn end
(shown at the bottom of the view) or message (shown at the top). The
newest turn end is skipped until it is answered, since it sits right
above the prompt. New keys previous_stop/next_stop (prefix+up/down) and
previous_input/next_input (prefix+shift+up/down) call it.

